# Code owners for purba.
#
# A branch ruleset cannot condition on a file path -- branch rulesets match ref
# names and repository properties only, and the "Restrict file paths" rule
# belongs to push rulesets, where it prevents a push rather than requiring an
# approval. So this file is the only native lever that scopes an approval to a
# directory, and it is why setting branch protection needed a pull request at
# all.
#
# The owner must hold write permission, and this file must be on the base
# branch of a pull request to have any effect.

/docs/decisions/ @snregales
/docs/README.md @snregales

# What a gate runs, the tools a job installs and the marks that start a gate
# are set here. A pull request that changes only one of these files changes a
# gate and touches no other path this file names.
/.config/ @snregales
/.cargo/ @snregales

# The gate lives here, and a pull request runs its own copy of it.
#   docs/decisions/liability-is-recorded-from-the-act-that-makes-it-true.md
#
# Half of it moved to `scripts/`, where a person runs it too. Without this line
# the code that decides every merge would be the only code here nobody owns.
/.github/ @snregales
/scripts/ @snregales
